**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
/target
# Alternate CARGO_TARGET_DIR used when running clippy alongside a build so the
# two don't thrash one cache. A build artefact dir — never committed.
/target-clippy
environments.json
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED. This workspace ships binaries operators build from
# source (e.g. the DID resolver cache server), and without a lockfile
# `--locked` has nothing to honour, so every clone resolves from scratch and
# inherits whatever upstream published that morning. That is how an
# `aws-smithy-types` MINOR release broke every mediator-setup wizard build in
# September 2026, when the mediator still lived here.
# The libraries published from here are unaffected: cargo ignores a dependency's
# lockfile, so this constrains only builds of this repository.
**/environments.json*

docs/*
# Architecture Decision Records are first-class, tracked docs.
!docs/adr/
# Security audit-readiness / threat-model docs are tracked.
!docs/security/
# Consumer migration guides are tracked.
!docs/migration/
# Testing guide + composed-stack docs are tracked.
!docs/testing/
# TSP usage cookbook is tracked.
!docs/tsp/
# Release runbooks for publishes that can't just be "merge and let CI run".
!docs/release/

# Secrets and bootstrap artifacts generated by the mediator-setup wizard (now in
# affinidi/affinidi-messaging-mediator). Kept ignored so a stray copy from an
# old checkout or a local run can never be committed.
**/conf/secrets.json
**/conf/secrets-admin.json
**/conf/keys/
**/bootstrap-request.json
**/bootstrap-request-vp.json
**/*.armor

# Superego
.superego/
CLAUDE.md
/docs/ssi-comparison-infographic.html

# Local agent state (Claude Code, etc.)
.claude/

# Secrets and credentials
.env
.env.*

# TSP interop harness build artifacts (standalone workspace)
interop/target/
